{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/neon/.codex/experiments/noodle84-20260917/issue-amended-smoke-fixture.json /Users/neon/.codex/experiments/noodle84-20260917/continuation-selection-attempt3.json'","aggregated_output":"{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/ed3c/noodle/issues/84\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/ed3c/noodle\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/ed3c/noodle/issues/84/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/ed3c/noodle/issues/84/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/ed3c/noodle/issues/84/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/ed3c/noodle/issues/84\",\"id\":5483874213,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOUIKUls8AAAABRt1HpQ\",\"number\":84,\"title\":\"Recover unpromoted stale initial proposals through one owner CLI continuation\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"ed3c\",\"id\":30064024,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMDY0MDI0\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30064024?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ed3c\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/ed3c\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ed3c/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ed3c/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ed3c/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ed3c/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ed3c/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ed3c/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ed3c/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ed3c/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/ed3c/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T06:35:00Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:21:25Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"OWNER\",\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"## One causal atom: safely retire an unpromoted initial-admission proposal\\n\\nUser requests a real Noodle order and a closed Issue atom that makes the P-class / CLI shortest continuation executable. Soodles #39 and #44 remain separate delivery atoms; do not fold their code, experiments or closure into this owner repair.\\n\\n### Trigger and current source\\nAt main `656e9ec73689c523058750e8b0a2388a15bb84fa`, initial admission rejects a stale revision or inconsistent completed-order projection and preserves `orders-next.json`, but no supported retirement continuation exists. Soodles' preserved proposal revision is `970e887025e1afec651ffdd8f8b42f76`; canonical revision is `dfb96fcf7d8d776ea177173c4c0c717d`. No Issue39 admission effect/worker exists. [Immutable failure evidence](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/tree/2c78b9151af96e3f6e6f52d9f0836a89942bb8da/docs/experiments/agent-context/delivery-blocked).\\n\\n### Owned correction and write boundary\\nNoodle owns one stopped-owner inspection/retirement entry for a definitively unpromoted rejected initial proposal. Reuse the existing instance lock, canonical-state readback, order parser, effect identity and process/session observation. Bind exact proposal digest and current canonical revision; preserve original bytes and refusal reason durably; unknown or admitted execution must remain refused. Inspect the completed-order projection mismatch in the same admission boundary and correct its producer/consumer only if the nearest discriminating control proves the causal defect; never weaken duplicate/admission guards.\\n\\nAllowed production boundary: root CLI registration and the new admission CLI file, `cmdmeta/` and `generate/` producers for the existing generated Noodle skill; `loop/` admission/recovery and nearest tests; existing `internal/lockfile`, canonical-state or process helpers only if the shared owner boundary requires them; the existing Noodle P-class skill and a bounded recovery recipe; narrowly related `brain/codebase` note and `docs/evidence/initial-admission-recovery` receipts. Existing tests may be corrected with the faulty implementation. No provider authority changes, credential broker, second scheduler, generic retry framework, manual snapshot/effect edits, or fabricated order completion.\\n\\n### Observable behavior\\n- One inspection entry returns structured owner, status, exact subject/revision, refusal reason, and supported `next` / exact operation inputs. The Session does not guess identity, permissions, state or recovery commands.\\n- A retirement requires unchanged input and exclusive owner access. Reject active loop/session, owned or admission-ledger subject, mismatched digest/revision and unreadable/ambiguous state. Preserve checkpoint, canonical ledger and evidence on every refusal.\\n- Persist attributable retirement intent/evidence before removing the mailbox. Actual process interruption before/after the persistence boundary resumes by owner readback with no second dispatch and without overwriting a later proposal.\\n- After retirement, return fresh canonical-readback/admission guidance. Retirement does not admit, restart or complete an order and cannot authorize provider writes.\\n\\n### N / P / L / R\\nN: this specification and reports. P: the shortest existing-entry recipe and recorded Session consumption. L: subject-bound gates, durable retirement/recovery, admission and quiescence checks. R: exact provider CI, merge and closure readbacks for this Noodle Issue. A green CLI or test cannot supply missing execution or provider truth.\\n\\n### Acceptance and actual order\\nRegister this Issue as a real Noodle order before its implementation writer starts, with measured local Codex carrier and native session/tool/Agent-produced typed outcome; no post-hoc empty order. Existing Noodle source control root is independent of the preserved Soodles production root. Use bounded observation and preserve actual child exits; missing outcomes remain incomplete.\\n\\nFor every new gate preserve defect RED, the same control corrected GREEN, and legal non-case GREEN. Reuse initial_admission_test.go controls; add actual child-process fault controls and exercise preserved A-completed → stale B input. A correct refusal is GREEN. Freeze external control/observer selection before final acceptance. Run `pnpm check` and exact-head provider Test under the repository contract; no disabled tests. Demonstrate a fresh Session consuming the CLI continuation without reconstructing argv or checkpoint and report actual actions, without claiming statistically proven cost reduction.\\n\\n### Delivery and cleanup\\nA supervised handoff preserves the original Noodle order/worktree identity and candidate commit. Read back exact-head checks, provider merge and Issue closure, then Noodle-owned completion/reconciliation and worktree cleanup; only then report this atom resolved. Do not use Soodles' hardcoded landing implementation to authorize a different repository. Preserve unknown writes and never replay them from memory. If the existing Noodle delivery entry cannot represent the requested order lifecycle, expose that concrete boundary rather than forging completion.\\n\\nThe repaired, independently accepted owner may then be explicitly pinned to inspect and recover the preserved Soodles proposal, retaining before/after receipts. That proves recovery only; Soodles #44 and #39 still require their own admissions and delivery receipts.\\n\\n### Observed verification-boundary correction (2026-09-17)\\nThe full `pnpm check` passed. The required smoke harness hardcodes `gpt-5.3-codex-spark`, which this actual ChatGPT carrier rejects before execution; its UI active-worktree control consequently times out. Preserve that failed run. Within this same acceptance boundary, permit the narrow model selection in `e2e/helpers_test.go` and `e2e/smoke_test.go` to use the already measured `gpt-6-astra` carrier, and rerun the unchanged behavioral controls. No skipped tests, relaxed UI assertions, new provider policy, or fabricated Agent results.\\n\\nA second real same-order attempt also exposed that baseline retry dispatch preserves the worktree path but runs `git checkout`/`git clean` on uncommitted progress. Both blocked attempts and source restoration evidence are retained. Do not requeue uncommitted work again. Finish and verify the candidate in the original worktree, persist a passing commit, then use the existing same-order continuation for independent completion verification; do not claim dirty-worktree recovery is fixed by this atom.\\n\\nThe user separately authorized an independent `verify-noodle` feature map in Soodles using pinned pstack create/maintain, referenced by its existing execute skill. That consumer has a separate repository/delivery boundary; its completion is not implied by this Noodle repair.\\n\\nSmoke follow-up evidence: after model alignment, the scheduler actually attempted `go run ./adapters/noodles-github schedule` inside a generic local fixture lacking that repository-specific adapter; INSTALL remained executing when its 120-second bound killed it. The same `e2e/helpers_test.go` / `e2e/smoke_test.go` acceptance boundary may correct fixture skills to the explicitly local backlog/task and pin onboarding inputs to this checkout, with bounded observation and unchanged UI/terminal assertions. Preserve both earlier failures. This verifies real local Noodle/Codex smoke, not GitHub adapter authorization or remote installation downloads.\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/ed3c/noodle/issues/84/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/ed3c/noodle/issues/84/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":{\"id\":1144995,\"client_id\":\"Iv23liVemv8A9if9v0F2\",\"slug\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\"node_id\":\"A_kwHOAOQ6Gs4AEXij\",\"owner\":{\"login\":\"openai\",\"id\":14957082,\"node_id\":\"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE0OTU3MDgy\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14957082?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/openai\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openai\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/openai/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/openai/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/openai/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/openai/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/openai/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/openai/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/openai/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/openai/received_events\",\"type\":\"Organization\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"name\":\"ChatGPT Codex Connector\",\"description\":\"Bring ChatGPT and Codex to your GitHub repositories.\",\"external_url\":\"https://www.chatgpt.com\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector\",\"created_at\":\"2025-02-14T01:37:05Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-20T16:37:15Z\",\"permissions\":{\"actions\":\"write\",\"checks\":\"read\",\"contents\":\"write\",\"emails\":\"read\",\"issues\":\"write\",\"metadata\":\"read\",\"pull_requests\":\"write\",\"statuses\":\"read\",\"workflows\":\"write\"},\"events\":[\"check_run\",\"check_suite\",\"commit_comment\",\"issues\",\"issue_comment\",\"pull_request\",\"pull_request_review\",\"pull_request_review_comment\",\"pull_request_review_thread\",\"repository\",\"status\",\"sub_issues\"]},\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null}\n{\n  \"order_id\": \"noodle-84\",\n  \"stage_index\": 0,\n  \"candidate_head\": \"5d1e9fefd902bec53b260b22abf3b55c3caf0203\",\n  \"task_sha256\": \"ceac1c81eb547ff57357c2d6aa833284db1cadaecd31724d7c28f986a9759950\",\n  \"binary\": \"/Users/neon/.codex/experiments/noodle78-delivery-20260916/control/.worktrees/issue84-control/.worktrees/noodle-84-0-execute/bin/noodle\",\n  \"binary_sha256\": \"85bd747fc7f408844b1c61199fa36a7b7e96cb02ffe9ac502e33fd9ca88e6919\",\n  \"skill\": \"/Users/neon/.codex/experiments/noodle78-delivery-20260916/control/.worktrees/issue84-control/.worktrees/noodle-84-0-execute/.agents/skills/noodle/SKILL.md\",\n  \"skill_sha256\": \"0dda11c1b839400686168505ce56cdd359e595ea78b9129a2761243959c496d0\",\n  \"cases\": {\n    \"stale-proposal\": \"/Users/neon/.codex/experiments/noodle84-20260917/attempt3-fixtures/stale-proposal\",\n    \"valid-proposal\": \"/Users/neon/.codex/experiments/noodle84-20260917/attempt3-fixtures/valid-proposal\"\n  },\n  \"fixture_digests_before\": {\n    \"stale-proposal\": {\n      \"orders-next.json\": \"c715406cd22b04ed125e6c7f98e8c2fa3267518e6ae5b84b46a9088c455b8088\",\n      \"orders.json\": \"5d3631b493687c08bebd5e39e19548dd94e713b6178e63799dc545d16c9f049b\",\n      \"state.snapshot.json\": \"3ef9e4f32535d5729c6eae0bf1de59c36c290c25e28ef467959e426bd330aee9\"\n    },\n    \"valid-proposal\": {\n      \"orders-next.json\": \"f4e3c252e98f7f30d00399410b07f99a1cafd93c3f194857f6abdd5dac5d2d23\",\n      \"orders.json\": \"5d3631b493687c08bebd5e39e19548dd94e713b6178e63799dc545d16c9f049b\",\n      \"state.snapshot.json\": \"3ef9e4f32535d5729c6eae0bf1de59c36c290c25e28ef467959e426bd330aee9\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"selected_at\": 1789630367.212597,\n  \"authorizes_landing\": false\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat .agents/skills/noodle/SKILL.md && rg --files /Users/neon/.codex/experiments/noodle84-20260917 | rg 'handoff|worker|journal' && rg --files brain | rg 'admission|prove-it-works|boundary-discipline|outcome-oriented'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat .agents/skills/noodle/SKILL.md && rg --files /Users/neon/.codex/experiments/noodle84-20260917 | rg 'handoff|worker|journal' && rg --files brain | rg 'admission|prove-it-works|boundary-discipline|outcome-oriented'\"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: noodle\ndescription: >-\n  Operate the Noodle CLI — explain commands, find flags, create/edit .noodle.toml config.\n  Also covers writing skills for Noodle: the orders pipeline, task-type schedule fields,\n  stage composition, and the orders-next.json schema. Use when running noodle commands,\n  editing .noodle.toml, writing or updating a skill's schedule field, or authoring new\n  task-type skills.\n---\n\n# Noodle\n\nSkills that run themselves. Write skills with a `schedule:` field describing when they should run. Noodle's scheduler agent reads those descriptions, writes orders, and the loop spawns agents in isolated worktrees to do the work.\n\n## How the Loop Works\n\n1. **Brief** — Noodle gathers project state into `.noodle/mise.json` (backlog, active agents, history, capacity, registered skills)\n2. **Schedule** — the scheduler agent reads mise, writes `.noodle/orders-next.json`\n3. **Dispatch** — Noodle promotes orders and spawns agent sessions\n4. **Execute** — each agent runs in its own worktree with the assigned skill\n5. **Merge** — completed work merges back to main\n\n## Skills\n\nA skill is a directory with a `SKILL.md`. The body is the agent's instructions. The frontmatter is metadata.\n\n**General skills** (no `schedule:`) are invoked directly by agents. Examples: `commit`, `debugging`.\n\n**Scheduled skills** (with `schedule:`) run autonomously. The scheduler reads the `schedule:` value as prose and uses judgment to decide when conditions are met.\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: quality\ndescription: Post-cook quality gate.\nschedule: \"Follow-up stage after execute. Cross-provider review preferred.\"\n---\n```\n\nSkills live in `.agents/skills/` by default. Paths in `skills.paths` are searched in order; first match wins.\n\nFor the full guide on writing skills, orders, and schedule fields, see [references/skill-authoring.md](references/skill-authoring.md).\n\n## Configuration\n\nNoodle reads `.noodle.toml` at project root. Scaffolded on first `noodle start`. Most projects only need:\n\n```toml\nmode = \"supervised\"  # auto | supervised | manual\n\n[routing.defaults]\nprovider = \"claude\"\nmodel = \"claude-opus-4-6\"\n\n[skills]\npaths = [\".agents/skills\"]\n```\n\nFull config reference: https://poteto.github.io/noodle/reference/configuration\n\n## CLI\n\nAll commands accept `--project-dir` (default: current directory, env: `NOODLE_PROJECT_DIR`).\n\n### Core\n\n| Command | Description |\n|---------|-------------|\n| `noodle start` | Start the noodle loop |\n| `noodle start --once` | Run one scheduling cycle and exit |\n| `noodle status` | Show runtime status (active agents, queue depth, loop state) |\n| `noodle reset` | Clear all runtime state (refuses if loop is running) |\n\n### Initial proposal recovery (P-class)\n\nUse the existing Noodle owner with a known project and a stopped loop.\nRun noodle --project-dir <known-project> admission inspect and consume its JSON.\nFor recoverable, execute next.argv exactly as an argv array. Never reconstruct\nthe digest, revision or command from memory or a historical checkpoint.\nFor refused, preserve evidence and report next.required to next.provided_by.\nAfter that owner resolves the condition, use next.readback_argv to inspect again.\nA valid initial proposal remains available for normal admission; do not retire it.\nFor retired, follow next.argv once for fresh canonical readback. For no_proposal,\nrecovery is finished: next.argv is empty and next names the scheduling owner\nand inputs for a separately admitted intent. Do not loop inspection indefinitely.\nRetirement does not dispatch, restart, complete an order or authorize provider\nwrites. Record the actual JSON, argv and operation results. Missing owner/project\ninputs must be supplied by the supervising operator, not guessed by the Session.\n\n| Command | Description |\n|---------|-------------|\n| noodle admission inspect | Inspect owner, subject, revision, invalid and exact next argv |\n| noodle admission retire PROPOSAL_SHA256 CURRENT_ORDER_REVISION | Archive and retire only the unchanged rejected initial proposal |\n\n### Skills & Schemas\n\n| Command | Description |\n|---------|-------------|\n| `noodle skills` | List resolved skills |\n| `noodle skills list` | List all resolved skills |\n| `noodle schema <target>` | Print schema docs for a target |\n| `noodle schema list` | List available schema targets (`mise`, `orders`, `status`) |\n\n### Worktrees\n\n| Command | Description |\n|---------|-------------|\n| `noodle worktree create <name>` | Create a new linked worktree |\n| `noodle worktree create <name> --from <ref>` | Create from a specific branch or commit |\n| `noodle worktree exec <name> <command...>` | Run a command inside a worktree (CWD-safe) |\n| `noodle worktree merge <name>` | Merge a worktree branch into integration branch |\n| `noodle worktree merge <name> --into <branch>` | Merge into a specific target branch |\n| `noodle worktree list` | List all worktrees with merge status |\n| `noodle worktree prune` | Remove merged and patch-equivalent worktrees |\n| `noodle worktree cleanup <name>` | Remove a worktree without merging |\n| `noodle worktree cleanup <name> --force` | Remove even with unmerged commits |\n| `noodle worktree hook` | Run worktree session hook (used internally) |\n\n### Events\n\n| Command | Description |\n|---------|-------------|\n| `noodle event emit <type>` | Emit an external event into the loop |\n| `noodle event emit <type> --payload <json>` | Emit with a JSON payload |\n| `noodle event emit <type> --session <id>` | Emit to a specific session's event log |\n\nFull CLI reference: https://poteto.github.io/noodle/reference/cli\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n1. **\"fatal config diagnostics prevent start\"** — Check `.noodle.toml` against `noodle schema`.\n2. **Missing adapter scripts** — Create scripts or update paths in config.\n3. **Stale worktrees** — `noodle worktree list`, then `noodle worktree prune`.\n\n## References\n\n- [references/skill-authoring.md](references/skill-authoring.md) — writing skills: pipeline, orders schema, schedule fields, stage composition, full examples\n- [references/configuration.md](references/configuration.md) — full .noodle.toml config reference\n- https://poteto.github.io/noodle/concepts/adapters — adapter setup, script contracts, provider examples\n- https://poteto.github.io/noodle/concepts/scheduling — how the loop schedules and dispatches work\n- https://poteto.github.io/noodle/concepts/skills — skill discovery, composition, scheduled vs general\n- https://poteto.github.io/noodle/concepts/runtimes — process, sprites, and runtime routing\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
